Often in Cicada 3301 you may encounter a puzzle or situation that needs a special technique or requires some repetitive task; below are a list compiled of different types of utilities that may be useful in these situations and during your solving.
__FORCETOC__

== Forewarning ==

Exercise caution while using any of these utilities. Anybody can freely add their own links here, so be careful when you download or run anything.

Uncovering-Cicada wiki takes no liability for any harm done by these utilities.

==Data translators==

These utilities translate information between different formats and number systems.

{{UtilityTable | 
{{UtilityEntry
|name=Paulschou's Xlate
|desc=Translates binary, ascii, hex, decimal, octal
|links=[https://paulschou.com/tools/xlate/ here]
|status=UP
}}
{{UtilityEntry
|name=Traductor
|desc=(Spanish Xlate) Translates binary, ascii, hex, decimal, octal
|links=[http://redir.dasumo.com/hex/ here]
|status=UP
}}
{{UtilityEntry
|name=JXlate
|desc=(Clientside Xlate) Website that translates multiple number and data systems
|links=[http://cyber.meme.tips/xlate/ here]
|status=UP
}}
{{UtilityEntry
|name=CyberChef
|desc=Website that allows multiple different steps to be used on data
|links=[https://gchq.github.io/CyberChef/ here]
|status=UP
}}
}}

==XOR utilities==

[[XOR]] is a reversible bitwise operation used in Cicada 3301 and other ARGs. These utilities make performing XOR between files easier in different ways.

{{UtilityTable | 
{{UtilityEntry
|name=JXlate
|desc=(Clientside Xlate) Translates multiple number and data systems
|links=[http://cyber.meme.tips/xlate/ here]
|status=UP
}}
{{UtilityEntry
|name=Skuater's XOR script
|desc=Unknown
|links=[https://infotomb.com/6ijx5 here]
|status=DEAD LINK
}}
{{UtilityEntry
|name=Cclark's XOR Script
|desc=XORs hex strings obtained from Cicada 3301 onion sites (Requires Python)
|links=[http://pastebin.com/nxXyrxin xor script] [http://pastebin.com/WM8RsWc0 permutation generator] [http://pastebin.com/T7KCsQcC permutations]
|status=UP
}}
{{UtilityEntry
|name=OTPXor
|desc=CLI utility for XORing two large files with with one offset, also provides text scanning modes.
|links=[https://github.com/otp22/decoders/tree/master/OtpXor here]
|status=UP
}}
{{UtilityEntry
|name=Nirsoft Xorfiles
|desc=Utility for xoring files in multiple combinations (WINE compatible)
|links=[http://www.nirsoft.net/utils/xorfiles.html here]
|status=UP
}}
{{UtilityEntry
|name=XorJ
|desc=GUI Program for XORing multiple files each at specified offsets and lengths. (Requires Java)
|links=[https://github.com/crashdemons/XorJ here]
|status=UP
}}
}}

==Rune manipulation==

As much of the documents provided by Cicada 3301 are in [[Runes Transcriptions|Runes]] or are encoded with the [[Gematria Primus]], these utilities make translating this associated information simpler.


{{UtilityTable |
{{UtilityEntry
|name=Huw's Rune Analyzer
|desc=Made in 2015 for the unsolved rune pages (explain) (Requires Python)
|links=[http://git.io/xQrlUg here]
|status=UP
}}
{{UtilityEntry
|name=Rune conversion script
|desc=Converts runes between primes values and letters (Requires Python)
|links=[http://pastebin.com/6v1XC1kV here]
|status=UP
}}
{{UtilityEntry
|name=Writing In Runes
|desc=Website that translates text into runes
|links=[http://the-oracle-answers.com/write-in-runes/ here]
|status=UP
}}
{{UtilityEntry
|name=Mlehmk's Rune Tool
|desc=Unfinished rune utility (explain) (Windows executable, Requires FreeMono font)
|links=[https://www.dropbox.com/s/8qybj9rlcd36x13/RuneShift.exe RuneShift.exe] [https://www.dropbox.com/s/5ix7rxn9kmb55dh/Rune.exe Rune.exe]
|images=[[File:Decryptor.png|thumb|200px]]
|status=UP
}}
{{UtilityEntry
|name=3301chef
|desc=Like cyberchef, allows multiple different steps to be used on data - but adds rune and gematria functions
|links=[http://opensource.exposed/ here] [https://gitlab.com/onecool/3301chef source]
|status=UP
}}
}}

==Text manipulation==

Basic text manipulation is still in use in some ciphers and puzzles, occasionally these utilities may be useful.

{{UtilityTable | 
{{UtilityEntry
|name=Anagram Solver
|desc=Website for finding hidden words in a phrase through anagrams
|links=[http://www.a2zwordfinder.com/anagram_solver.html here]
|status=UP
}}
{{UtilityEntry
|name=Reverse Text
|desc=Website for generating reversed text
|links=[http://textmechanic.com/Reverse-Text-Generator.html here]
|status=UP
}}
{{UtilityEntry
|name=Rumkin Ciphers
|desc=Website featuring various useful classical text ciphers
|links=[http://rumkin.com/tools/cipher/index.php here]
|status=UP
}}
}}

==Steganography==

More often than not in Cicada 3301, there are images or files that store hidden information - these tools help to reveal it.

{{UtilityTable | 
{{UtilityEntry
|name=JJTC Stegonography tools
|desc=Various tools for steganography
|links=[http://www.jjtc.com/Steganography/tools.html here]
|status=UP
}}
{{UtilityEntry
|name=Outguess
|desc=Program for embedding and retrieving encrypted messages in JPEG images
|links=[https://github.com/crorvick/outguess here]
|status=UP
}}
{{UtilityEntry
|name=OpenPuff
|desc=Another Steg utility supporting multiple file formats
|links=[http://embeddedsw.net/OpenPuff_Steganography_Home.html here]
|status=UP
}}
}}

==File analysis==

These utilities provide information about file formats, statistical analysis or reveal metadata about them.

{{UtilityTable | 
{{UtilityEntry
|name=EXIF Tool
|desc=Website for revealing various forms of metadata in images and other file formats
|links=[http://exif.regex.info/exif.cgi here]
|status=UP
}}
{{UtilityEntry
|name=JPDump
|desc=Website that outputs and allows downloading header information from image files.
|links=[http://cyber.meme.tips/jpdump/ here]
|status=UP
}}
}}

